    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit that rejects with **429 Too Many Requests** when 100 or more owners have already been registered today (by `registrationDate`).\n\nFollowing the existing patterns in the codebase (mirroring the `CityAtCapacityException` per-city cap):\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when the daily cap is hit.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added `handleDailyOwnerLimitException`, which maps the exception to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `requireDailyLimitNotReached()` check (after required-field validation, before the other business-rule checks). It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count is `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100). Since new owners default to today's `registrationDate`, this caps creations at 100/day and rejects the 101st.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` test (create 100, then the 101st is rejected) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
